    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m facing really strange dplyr::summarise behavior, and I can&#39;t tell whether it&#39;s something intentional that I don&#39;t understand, or a bug. Here&#39;s the data I&#39;m working with, and a brief description.<div><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">library(dplyr)</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">info &lt;- read.delim(&quot;<a href=\"http://jofrhwld.github.io/assets/audio_stats.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jofrhwld.github.io/assets/audio_stats.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792358102368000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_HlNKQisilXNikzoPs1lw\">http://jofrhwld.github.io/assets/audio_stats.txt</a>&quot;)</font></div></div></blockquote><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">glimpse(info)</font></div></blockquote><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># Variables:</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># $ transcribed (dbl) 2810.733, 2813.321, 3706.089, 2777.893, 2739.913, 1200.568, 483.747, 904....</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># $ total       (dbl) 2814.345, 2826.450, 3717.926, 3957.084, 2758.806, 2587.360, 492.168, 3799...</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># $ nvowels     (int) 3078, 3702, 5885, 3884, 4119, 1471, 258, 859, 3213, 1396, 836, 2565, 1585... </font></div></blockquote><div><div><br></div></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">sum(info$total)/3600</font></div></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># 257.3137</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">sum(info$transcribed)/3600</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># 198.201</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">sum(info$nvowels)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># 629069</font></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div> </div><div>I&#39;m running into the summarise error here:</div><div><br></div></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">info %&gt;% summarise(</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    Total = sum(total)/3600,</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    Transcribed = sum(transcribed)/3600,</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    Vowels = formatC(sum(nvowels), big.mark = &quot;,&quot;)</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  )</font></div></div></div></blockquote><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">#      Total Transcribed Vowels</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># 1 257.3137   0.7807592  3,078</font></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>That&#39;s totally wrong, but I have no idea why. If I drop out the first column, the Transcribed number is correct.</div><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">info %&gt;% summarise(</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    #Total = sum(total)/3600,</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    Transcribed = sum(transcribed)/3600,</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    Vowels = formatC(sum(nvowels), big.mark = &quot;,&quot;)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  )</font></div></blockquote><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">#   Transcribed Vowels</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># 1     198.201  3,078</font></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>And if I drop out the Transcribed column also, the Vowels number is correct.</div><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">info %&gt;% summarise(</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    #Total = sum(total)/3600,</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    #Transcribed = sum(transcribed)/3600,</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    Vowels = formatC(sum(nvowels), big.mark = &quot;,&quot;)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  )</font> </div></blockquote><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">#    Vowels</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># 1 629,069</font></div></div></div></blockquote><div><div><br></div><div>And for some reason, if I drop the formatC from the original call, the Vowels column is now correct.</div><div><br></div></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">info %&gt;% summarise(</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    Total = sum(total)/3600,</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    Transcribed = sum(transcribed)/3600,</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    Vowels = sum(nvowels)</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  )</font></div></div></div></blockquote><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">#      Total Transcribed Vowels</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"># 1 257.3137   0.7807592 629069</font></div></div></div></blockquote><div><div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t know why these columns should be interacting with each other. Here&#39;s my sessionInfo, fwiw</div><div><br></div></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">R version 3.0.2 (2013-09-25)</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Platform: x86_64-apple-darwin10.8.0 (64-bit)</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">locale:</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">[1] en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/C/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">attached base packages:</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     </font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">other attached packages:</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">[1] dplyr_0.2.0.99</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">loaded via a namespace (and not attached):</font></div></div></div><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">[1] assertthat_0.1 magrittr_1.0.1 parallel_3.0.2 Rcpp_0.11.1    tools_3.0.2 </font></div></div></div><div><div><br></div></div></blockquote><div><div>-Joe</div></div></div>"
    ]
